---Represents an Electrocardiogram (ECG) measurement session. This data type is based on SaMD feature and any changes to it may require additional review.
---@class gcp.health_v4.Electrocardiogram
---@field beatsPerMinuteAvg? string Optional. Average heart rate recorded during ECG reading in beats per minute.
---@field waveformSamples? gcp.health_v4.IntegerList Optional. An array of voltage values representing lead I ECG values. Each sample represents voltage difference in ECG graph. The first value in array corresponds to the start of the reading.
---@field samplingFrequencyHertz? number Optional. The sampling frequency of waveform samples in hertz.
---@field leadNumber? number Optional. The number of leads used for ECG reading.
---@field medicalDeviceInfo? gcp.health_v4.MedicalDeviceInfo Output only. The meta information for the compatible device used to conduct the measurement. ECG measurements typically populate `firmware_version`, `feature_version`, and `device_model`.
---@field interval? gcp.health_v4.SessionTimeInterval Required. Observed interval. NOTE: Historical ECG data lacks timezone offsets, so `start_utc_offset` and `end_utc_offset` will be missing or default to zero. As a result, the civil time fields within this interval will default to UTC. It is recommended to use physical time fields instead for accurate time referencing. NOTE: The `start_time` and `end_time` of the interval are equal, representing the reading time.
---@field resultClassification? gcp.health_v4.ElectrocardiogramResultClassificationEnum|string Optional. The result classification of the ECG reading.
---@field millivoltsScalingFactor? number Optional. The factor by which to divide waveform samples to get voltage in millivolts: millivolts = waveform_sample / millivolts_scaling_factor.

---@alias gcp.health_v4.ElectrocardiogramResultClassificationEnum "RESULT_CLASSIFICATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL_SINUS_RHYTHM"|"ATRIAL_FIBRILLATION"|"INCONCLUSIVE"|"INCONCLUSIVE_HIGH_HEART_RATE"|"INCONCLUSIVE_LOW_HEART_RATE"|"UNREADABLE"|"NOT_ANALYZED"

---A generic empty message that you can re-use to avoid defining duplicated empty messages in your APIs. A typical example is to use it as the request or the response type of an API method. For instance: service Foo { rpc Bar(google.protobuf.Empty) returns (google.protobuf.Empty); }
---@class gcp.health_v4.Empty

---Authorization mechanism for a subscriber endpoint. For all requests sent by the Webhooks service, the JSON payload is cryptographically signed. The signature is delivered in the `GOOGLE-HEALTH-API-SIGNATURE` HTTP header. This is an ECDSA (NIST P256) signature of the JSON payload. Clients must verify this signature using Google Health API's public key to confirm the payload was sent by the Health API.
---@class gcp.health_v4.EndpointAuthorization
---@field secretSet? boolean Output only. Whether the secret is set.
---@field secret? string Required. Input only. Provides a client-provided secret that will be sent with each notification to the subscriber endpoint using the "Authorization" header. The value must include the authorization scheme, e.g., "Bearer " or "Basic ", as it will be used as the full Authorization header value. This secret is used by the API to test the endpoint during `CreateSubscriber` and `UpdateSubscriber` calls, and will be sent in the `Authorization` header for all subsequent webhook notifications to this endpoint.

